                <pb facs="0179" n="71" sameAs="frus:frus1927v02/pg71"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/8207: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-02-08T13:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 8,
                                1927—1 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received February 8—6:44
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>121. My 119, February 7, 5 p.m. Following from American consul general at Hankow:
                        <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“February 7, 11 a.m. My February 6, 2 p.m. General Chu, Chief of Staff,
                            informs me this morning that he has referred memorandum to Minister for
                            Foreign Affairs, which procedure was no doubt promptly arranged by Ch’en
                            after I saw him yesterday.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
